---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Canadian Anti-Dumping Duties on Food Packaging: Sourcing Options from Corncomp';
const description = 'Compare paper food packaging production in China, Cambodia and Canada, and check Canadian trade-duty exposure before ordering.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title + ' | Corncomp'} description={description} pathname="/design-preview/canada-packaging/" bodyClass="architecture-site">
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex" slot="head" />
  <article class="content-shell content-post blog-article">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/design-preview/blog/">Blog preview</a></nav>
    <header class="blog-article__hero">
      <div class="content-heading"><h1>{title}</h1></div>
      <figure class="blog-article__cover"><img src="/media/about/blog-canada-packaging.webp" width="1440" height="810" alt="Kraft salad bowl with a clear lid against a red maple-leaf paper collage" fetchpriority="high" /></figure>
    </header>
    <div class="blog-article__reading">
      <div class="wordpress-content blog-article__body">
        <p><strong>Corncomp is a Chinese paper food packaging manufacturer with factories in China, Cambodia and Canada. All three factories can produce paper cups, paper salad bowls and paper straws.</strong> Canadian buyers can request quotes by manufacturing location to compare lead times and landed costs. When an imported option carries trade-duty exposure, ask for a quote for Canadian production as well.</p>
        <h2>Which Canadian trade measures should packaging buyers check?</h2>
        <p>The Canada Border Services Agency (CBSA) has a proceeding on certain paperboard cups and containers originating in or exported from China. It separately lists a measure in force for certain thermoformed molded fibre tableware from China. Before ordering, check the current status and compare the exact item with the applicable product definition. <a href="https://cbsa-asfc.gc.ca/sima-lmsi/i-e/pcc2026/pcc2026-ni-eng.html">CBSA paperboard cups and containers proceeding</a> · <a href="https://cbsa-asfc.gc.ca/sima-lmsi/mif-mev/tmft-eng.html">CBSA molded fibre tableware measure</a></p>
        <p>For a biodegradability or compostability claim, request evidence for the finished item. For trade duties, have your Canadian customs broker review the product construction, origin and country of export. When the scope of a measure in force is unclear, the CBSA provides a formal scope-ruling process. <a href="https://cbsa-asfc.gc.ca/sima-lmsi/sp-pp-eng.html">CBSA scope proceedings</a></p>
        <h2>How can Corncomp’s three factories help Canadian buyers?</h2>
        <table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Manufacturing location</th><th scope="col">What to check before ordering</th></tr></thead><tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">China</th><td>Confirm the SKU, coating or lining and proposed exporter. Have your broker check the applicable proceeding and duty exposure.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Cambodia</th><td>Request a quote for actual production in Cambodia. Confirm the manufacturing steps and available origin documents with your broker.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Canada</th><td>Request a domestic production quote for the same finished item. Confirm the specification, production lead time and delivery cost to your Canadian warehouse.</td></tr>
        </tbody></table>
        <p>For a kraft salad bowl with a matching lid, give each factory the same bowl volume, dimensions, lining and lid material. Quote each location separately so your broker can assess the imported options using the details for that shipment. The Canadian importer accounts for applicable SIMA duties. <a href="https://cbsa-asfc.gc.ca/sima-lmsi/self-auto-eng.html">CBSA guide to self-assessing SIMA duties</a></p>
        <h2>How do I request a quote for a Canadian order?</h2>
        <p>Send the SKU or product photo, dimensions or capacity, material and lining requirements, intended use, order quantity, Canadian delivery location and target delivery date. Ask for the proposed manufacturing site and lead time on each quote. <a href="/contact/">Request a quote from Corncomp</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
